---
description: Comments for non-trivial logic in firmware C
globs: ["**/*.c", "**/*.h"]
---

# Commenting

Comment non-trivial logic with `/* */`. Explain why it exists: constraints,
edge cases, hardware limits, expected inputs. Do not restate the next line.
Place the comment directly above the code (or trailing if it fits one line).
State the implementation; do not contrast it with an alternative. Avoid using
"X is not Y, but Z" or "This is done because X instead of Y" phrasing.

```c
/* BAD: restates the assignment */
TIM16->PSC = 15;

/* BAD: contrast phrasing */
/* Prescaler is not 8; it is 16 so the tick is 1 MHz. */
TIM16->PSC = 15;

/* GOOD: why this value exists */
/* 16 MHz / 16 = 1 MHz tick for microsecond delays. */
TIM16->PSC = 15;
```

Avoid leaving comments that are only relevant to the narrow context of the
fix performed.

```c
/* BAD: leftover from moving the define in this change */
/* Was in flash_ll.h; IAP needed it so it lives here now. */
#define FLASH_FW_PAGE0      (BL_SIZE / FLASH_PAGE_SIZE)

/* GOOD: why this value exists */
/* First page of the firmware slot. */
#define FLASH_FW_PAGE0      (BL_SIZE / FLASH_PAGE_SIZE)
```
